From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PonWrt <noreply@localhost>
Date: Fri, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: grow PON RX rings within the memory budget

Increase the PON rings 21..23 to 1024 descriptors and the CPU/control rings
2/4/11/15 to 256. Keep the LRO rings 24..30 at 64 descriptors because each
uses a 16 KiB page: applying the original 1024-descriptor candidate to them
would add about 235.5 MiB on AN7581's two QDMAs.

The selected profile adds about 24.3 MiB including RX buffers, descriptor
memory and queue metadata. Raise the page pool to cover the largest ring.

Source: pbs05/ponwrt issue #41 embedded diff.
Link: https://github.com/pbs05/ponwrt/issues/41
Signed-off-by: PonWrt <noreply@localhost>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 2 +-
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h | 7 ++++++-
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1182,7 +1182,7 @@
 				     struct airoha_qdma *qdma, int ndesc)
 {
 	struct page_pool_params pp_params = {
-		.pool_size = 256,
+		.pool_size = 1024,
 		.flags = PP_FLAG_DMA_MAP | PP_FLAG_DMA_SYNC_DEV,
 		.dma_dir = DMA_FROM_DEVICE,
 		.nid = NUMA_NO_NODE,
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -41,11 +41,12 @@
 #define IRQ_QUEUE_LEN(_n)		((_n) ? 1024 : 2048)
 #define TX_DSCP_NUM			1024
 #define RX_DSCP_NUM(_n)			\
-	((_n) ==  2 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) ==  4 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) == 11 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) == 15 ? 128 :		\
-	 (_n) ==  0 ? 1024 : 32)
+	((_n) ==  0 ? 1024 :		\
+	 (_n) >= 21 && (_n) <= 23 ? 1024 : \
+	 (_n) ==  2 ? 256 :		\
+	 (_n) ==  4 ? 256 :		\
+	 (_n) == 11 ? 256 :		\
+	 (_n) == 15 ? 256 : 64)
 
 #define AIROHA_LRO_PAGE_ORDER		get_order(SZ_16K)
 #define AIROHA_MAX_NUM_LRO_QUEUES	8
